	year = {1968},
	issn = {0038-5646},
	keywords = {Quantum theory; },
	language = {Russian},
	abstract = {Relaxation of a quantum harmonic oscillator to the thermodynamic equilibrium state is considered on basis of a kinetic equation. The method of generating functions is employed for solving the equation. A number of exact solutions for various initial conditions is considered. For large quantum numbers it can be transformed to the Fokker-Planck equation. The Green function for the latter is determined. It is shown how the results obtained can be applied to the problem of statistics of photocounts. The given kinetic equation is extended to the case when an external classical force f(t) which arbitrarily depends on time acts on the oscillator. Methods for describing the evolution of the oscillator (characteristic functions, distributions of quasiprobabilities on the alpha plane) are briefly considered. The methods are valid in the presence of a force f(t). The equations of motion of the corresponding quantities are derived. The partial solutions for the density matrix rho are presented in a table. The so-called 'harmonic oscillator paradox' is discussed.}
}

